---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout 
  title="How Much Does a Website Cost in Shelby, NC? (2026 Pricing Guide)"
  description="Complete 2026 pricing guide for web design in Shelby, NC. Learn what actually drives website costs, realistic price ranges, and questions to ask before hiring."
>
  <article class="pt-32 pb-24 px-4">
    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
      <!-- Header -->
      <header class="mb-16 text-center">
        <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-3 mb-6 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full border border-brand-cyan/20 bg-brand-cyan/5">
          <span class="text-brand-cyan text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-widest">Vol #2 Article #13</span>
          <span class="w-1 h-1 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/30"></span>
          <span class="text-brand-sky/60 text-xs font-medium uppercase tracking-widest">August 2026</span>
        </div>
        <h1 class="font-heading text-5xl md:text-7xl font-black text-white mb-8 tracking-tight leading-[1.1]">
          How Much Does a Website Cost in <br />
          <span class="text-transparent bg-clip-text bg-gradient-to-r from-brand-cyan to-brand-blue">Shelby, NC? (2026 Pricing Guide)</span>
        </h1>
        <p class="text-xl md:text-2xl text-brand-sky/80 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mx-auto">
          If you've started researching web design in Shelby, NC, you've probably noticed the honest answer isn't a single number. This guide breaks down what actually drives cost, realistic price ranges, and the questions worth asking before you hire anyone.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Main Image Placeholder -->
      <div class="aspect-video bg-brand-dark border border-white/5 rounded-3xl mb-16 overflow-hidden shadow-2xl relative group">
        <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-blue/20 to-transparent opacity-50 group-hover:opacity-70 transition-opacity"></div>
        <div class="absolute inset-0 flex items-center justify-center">
           <span class="text-brand-sky/20 font-heading text-4xl font-bold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] transform -rotate-12">Shelby Web Company Official</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Content -->
      <div class="prose prose-invert prose-2xl max-w-none">
        <p class="text-lg text-brand-sky/90 mb-12">
          <a href="/" class="text-brand-cyan hover:underline decoration-brand-cyan/30 underline-offset-4">Shelby Web Company</a> creates web design Shelby that turns visitors into customers.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">The Short Answer</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8">
          Pricing for a Shelby-area small business site typically runs <strong class="text-white">$598</strong> (the lowest end of our pricing spectrum) to <strong class="text-white">$3,998</strong> to build, depending on how much site you actually need — with most growing businesses landing around <strong class="text-white">$1,298</strong> average for a professional package built with SEO baked in to actually generate leads, not just look nice. On top of that, ongoing care (hosting, backups, and updates) runs <strong class="text-white">$75–$149/month</strong>. Where you land in that range depends less on "how many pages" and more on a handful of specific factors below.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">What Actually Drives the Price</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="space-y-8 mb-16">
          <div class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 hover:border-brand-blue/20 transition-all">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">1. Which package actually fits the goal</h3>
            <p class="text-brand-sky/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">Our Starter package ($598) covers a clean 1–5 page brochure site — great for a simple online presence, but it's not built to actively generate leads. Most businesses that want real lead flow move up to the Professional Business tier, where custom UI/UX, stronger forms, and local SEO are baked in.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 hover:border-brand-blue/20 transition-all">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">2. Number of pages and complexity</h3>
            <p class="text-brand-sky/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">A simple brochure site (Home, About, Services, Contact) sits at the low end. A 5–10 page site with a blog, stronger lead-capture forms, and full analytics — our most popular option — climbs into the Professional Business range. Add e-commerce, booking, or CRM integrations and you're into Scale Business territory.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 hover:border-brand-blue/20 transition-all">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">3. Content: who's writing and shooting it</h3>
            <p class="text-brand-sky/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">Professional copywriting and photography aren't required, but they show. If you need your web designer and/or developer to also write your page content or arrange a photo shoot, that's typically a separate line item from the design/development work itself.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 hover:border-brand-blue/20 transition-all">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">4. SEO and local search setup</h3>
            <p class="text-brand-sky/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">A site that just exists and a site that's actually built to show up when someone searches "web design shelby" or "[your service] near me" are two different projects. Proper on-page SEO, Google Business Profile setup, and local schema markup take extra time upfront but are usually what separates a website that generates leads from one that just sits there.</p>
          </div>
          
          <div class="bg-brand-dark/50 p-8 rounded-2xl border border-white/5 hover:border-brand-blue/20 transition-all">
            <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-white mb-4">5. Ongoing hosting, maintenance, and support</h3>
            <p class="text-brand-sky/70 text-sm leading-relaxed">Almost every website needs some level of ongoing care — hosting, backups, code updates, and small revisions so the site stays secure and current. We offer two Website Care Plan tiers: Basic ($75/mo) covers hosting, backups, and core code updates, while Premium ($149/mo) adds more frequent revisions and a higher level of ongoing support. Most Shelby-area business owners prefer having this handled rather than trying to manage hosting and updates themselves.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">Typical Price Ranges</span>
        </h2>

        <div class="bg-brand-dark border border-white/5 p-8 rounded-3xl mb-16 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left min-w-[600px]">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                <th class="text-brand-cyan font-bold pb-4">Package</th>
                <th class="text-brand-cyan font-bold pb-4">Price</th>
                <th class="text-brand-cyan font-bold pb-4">Best for</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-brand-sky/80">
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-4 font-medium text-white">Starter Website</td>
                <td class="py-4">$598</td>
                <td class="py-4 text-sm">A simple 1–5 page brochure site with basic SEO. Budget-friendly, but not built to actively generate leads — think of it as a digital business card, not a growth engine.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-4 font-medium text-white">Professional Business Suite (most popular)</td>
                <td class="py-4">$998 – $1,998 (avg. ~$1,298)</td>
                <td class="py-4 text-sm">A 5–10 page custom site with local SEO, stronger lead-capture forms, and analytics. This is what most Shelby-area businesses trying to actually grow should budget for.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-4 font-medium text-white">Scale Business</td>
                <td class="py-4">$2,000 – $3,998</td>
                <td class="py-4 text-sm">10–20 pages, full blog/content strategy, CRM integrations, and e-commerce or booking — built for multi-service or multi-location businesses.</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-4 font-medium text-white">Enterprise / Custom</td>
                <td class="py-4">Custom quote</td>
                <td class="py-4 text-sm">Fully custom web applications, membership portals, and advanced integrations for complex operations.</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-brand-blue/5 border-l-4 border-brand-blue p-8 my-12 rounded-r-2xl">
          <p class="text-white font-medium italic mb-0">A quick honest note on the Starter tier: at $598, it's a great low-cost way to get a professional presence online fast — but if generating leads and ranking locally is the goal, the Professional Business package is where the local SEO, stronger forms, and analytics actually kick in. That's why most businesses serious about growth land in the $998–$1,998 range, averaging around $1,298.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">Don't Forget Ongoing Care</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8">
          The build cost above covers getting your site live — but a website isn't a "set it and forget it" purchase. Hosting, backups, and code updates keep it secure, fast, and functioning as browsers and plugins change over time. We offer two Website Care Plan tiers to handle this for you:
        </p>

        <div class="bg-brand-dark border border-white/5 p-8 rounded-3xl mb-16 overflow-x-auto">
          <table class="w-full text-left min-w-[600px]">
            <thead>
              <tr class="border-b border-white/10">
                <th class="text-brand-cyan font-bold pb-4">Care Plan</th>
                <th class="text-brand-cyan font-bold pb-4">Price</th>
                <th class="text-brand-cyan font-bold pb-4">What's covered</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody class="text-brand-sky/80">
              <tr class="border-b border-white/5">
                <td class="py-4 font-medium text-white">Basic Website Care</td>
                <td class="py-4">$75/mo</td>
                <td class="py-4 text-sm">Web hosting, backups, and core code updates to keep your site secure and running smoothly</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <td class="py-4 font-medium text-white">Premium Website Care</td>
                <td class="py-4">$149/mo</td>
                <td class="py-4 text-sm">Everything in Basic, plus more frequent revisions and a higher level of ongoing support</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-brand-accent/5 border-l-4 border-brand-accent p-8 my-12 rounded-r-2xl">
          <p class="text-white font-medium italic mb-0">Think of this the same way you'd think of an oil change for a car you just bought — the build cost gets you on the road, the care plan is what keeps it running well for years instead of breaking down six months in.</p>
        </div>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">Questions to Ask Before You Hire Anyone</span>
        </h2>
        
        <ul class="space-y-6 list-none p-0 mb-16">
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">?</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Is SEO included, or is that a separate cost?</strong>
              <span class="text-brand-sky/70">A cheap site that never shows up in Google search isn't actually cheap.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">?</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Who owns the website once it's built?</strong>
              <span class="text-brand-sky/70">Make sure you retain ownership of your domain and site files, not just "access" to them.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">?</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">What happens after launch, and what does it cost monthly?</strong>
              <span class="text-brand-sky/70">Ask exactly what a care plan includes — hosting, backups, and updates should be clearly spelled out, not vague.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">?</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">Can I see local examples?</strong>
              <span class="text-brand-sky/70">A designer who's worked with businesses in Cleveland County will understand your customer base — and your competition — better than someone who's never been to Shelby.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
          <li class="flex gap-4">
            <div class="shrink-0 w-8 h-8 rounded-full bg-brand-cyan/10 border border-brand-cyan/20 flex items-center justify-center text-brand-cyan font-bold text-sm">?</div>
            <div>
              <strong class="text-white block mb-1">What's the timeline?</strong>
              <span class="text-brand-sky/70">A realistic small-business site typically takes 3–6 weeks from kickoff to launch, depending on how quickly content and feedback come together.</span>
            </div>
          </li>
        </ul>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">Getting Started Doesn't Have to Be Stressful</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8">
          One thing worth knowing upfront: you don't need to pay the full project cost out of pocket on day one. We keep the process simple with a straightforward 50/50 split — 50% down to kick off the project, and 50% due upon completion. Flexible payment plans are also available if that works better for your business.
        </p>

        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8">
          This isn't just about easing the financial entry — it keeps both sides invested in the project from start to finish, which tends to make for a smoother, more focused build than an all-upfront or all-on-delivery arrangement.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">The Real Cost of Not Investing</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-8">
          It's worth flipping the question: what does it cost your business to not have a website that ranks locally? Every month a Shelby customer searches for what you do and finds a competitor first is a lead you never even got a chance to compete for. A website isn't really the expense — it's the storefront that's open and findable 24/7, even when your shop isn't.
        </p>

        <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-white mt-16 mb-8 flex items-center gap-4">
          <span class="text-brand-accent">Get a Real Number for Your Business</span>
        </h2>
        
        <p class="text-brand-sky/80 mb-12">
          Every business is different, and the fastest way to get an accurate quote is a quick conversation with us about what you actually need. Contact Shelby Web Co. for a free, no-pressure quote, or take a look at our web design services to see what's included at each level.
        </p>

        <p class="text-brand-sky/60 text-sm mb-12">
          Shelby Web Co. designs and builds websites for small businesses throughout Shelby, Gastonia, Forest City, Boiling Springs, and Polkville and Asheville, NC — with local SEO built in from day one, not tacked on after the fact.
        </p>

        <!-- CTA Section -->
        <div class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-blue to-brand-dark p-12 rounded-[2rem] text-center relative overflow-hidden">
          <div class="absolute inset-0 bg-[radial-gradient(circle_at_50%_50%,rgba(132,204,22,0.1),transparent_70%)]"></div>
          <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-black text-white mb-6 relative z-10">Ready to Get Your Website Quote?</h2>
          <p class="text-xl text-white/80 mb-10 relative z-10 max-w-2xl mx-auto">
            Let's talk about what your business actually needs and get you an accurate, no-pressure quote.
          </p>
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center relative z-10">
            <a href="/contact" class="cta-glow-shine bg-brand-accent text-[#0A0A0A] px-10 py-4 rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:bg-brand-accent-light">
              Get Your Free Quote
            </a>
            <a href="tel:7044738188" class="bg-white/10 backdrop-blur-md text-white border border-white/20 px-10 py-4 rounded-xl font-bold text-lg hover:bg-white/20 transition-all flex items-center justify-center gap-2">
              <svg class="w-5 h-5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M3 5a2 2 0 012-2h3.28a1 1 0 01.948.684l1.498 4.493a1 1 0 01-.502 1.21l-2.257 1.13a11.042 11.042 0 005.516 5.516l1.13-2.257a1 1 0 011.21-.502l4.493 1.498a1 1 0 01.684.949V19a2 2 0 01-2 2h-1C9.716 21 3 14.284 3 6V5z"/></svg>
              (704) 473-8188
            </a>
          </div>
          <p class="text-white/40 text-sm mt-8 relative z-10">
            Limited-Time Offer: Free logo design + $100 referral bonus with any website package.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Footer navigation -->
      <footer class="mt-24 pt-12 border-t border-white/5 flex flex-wrap gap-8 items-center justify-between">
        <a href="/blog" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors flex items-center gap-2">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24"><path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M15 19l-7-7 7-7"/></svg>
          Back to Blog
        </a>
        <div class="flex gap-6">
          <a href="/" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors">Home</a>
          <a href="/services/web-design" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors">Web Design</a>
          <a href="/contact" class="text-brand-sky/60 hover:text-white transition-colors">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </footer>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
